{"id":"62a46f3922b57bd0","group":"58","path":"58/batch14/58-thm-easton.md","title":"Easton's Theorem","display":"thm-easton — Easton's Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-easton","aliases":["58-thm-easton"],"display":"thm-easton — Easton's Theorem","depends_on":["[[../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-easton"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-easton</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-easton — Easton's Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" href=\"?note=a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" title=\"../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md\">../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbf V\">\\(\\mathbf V\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbf W\">\\(\\mathbf W\\)</span> denote proper-class universes in the ambient class metatheory; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F,\\mathbb P,G\">\\(F,\\mathbb P,G\\)</span> are class parameters rather than elements of the set universe.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZFC}\">\\(\\mathrm{ZFC}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{GCH}\">\\(\\mathrm{GCH}\\)</span> denote the usual axiom theory and generalized-continuum sentence schema.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(\\mathbf V,\\in)\\models_{\\mathsf{Cls}}\\mathrm{ZFC+GCH}\">\\((\\mathbf V,\\in)\\models_{\\mathsf{Cls}}\\mathrm{ZFC+GCH}\\)</span> is the class-satisfaction schema for the ground universe.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{DefinableEastonFunction}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(F,\\mathbf V)\">\\(\\mathrm{DefinableEastonFunction}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(F,\\mathbf V)\\)</span> means that <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F\">\\(F\\)</span> is a definable amenable class function from the infinite regular cardinals of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbf V\">\\(\\mathbf V\\)</span> to its cardinals, is monotone there, and satisfies <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa&lt;\\operatorname{cf}^{\\mathbf V}(F(\\kappa))\">\\(\\kappa&lt;\\operatorname{cf}^{\\mathbf V}(F(\\kappa))\\)</span> for every such <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{EastonClassForcingExtension}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(\\mathbf W,\\mathbf V,\\mathbb P,G)\">\\(\\mathrm{EastonClassForcingExtension}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(\\mathbf W,\\mathbf V,\\mathbb P,G)\\)</span> means that <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb P\">\\(\\mathbb P\\)</span> is the Easton-support class forcing determined by <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F\">\\(F\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"G\">\\(G\\)</span> is generic over <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbf V\">\\(\\mathbf V\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbf W=\\mathbf V[G]\">\\(\\mathbf W=\\mathbf V[G]\\)</span> is its tame class-forcing extension.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}easton} \\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n(\\mathbf V,\\in)\\models_{\\mathsf{Cls}}\\mathrm{ZFC}\\mathbin{+}\\mathrm{GCH}\\land\n\\mathrm{DefinableEastonFunction}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(F,\\mathbf V)\n\\to\\exists_{\\mathsf{Cls}}\\mathbf W,\\mathbb P,G\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{EastonClassForcingExtension}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(\\mathbf W,\\mathbf V,\\mathbb P,G)\\land\n(\\mathbf W,\\in)\\models_{\\mathsf{Cls}}\\mathrm{ZFC}\\land\n\\operatorname{Ord}^{\\mathbf W}=\\operatorname{Ord}^{\\mathbf V}\\land\n\\operatorname{Card}^{\\mathbf W}=\\operatorname{Card}^{\\mathbf V}\\land\n\\forall\\alpha\\in\\operatorname{Ord}^{\\mathbf V}\\;\n\\bigl(\\operatorname{cf}^{\\mathbf W}(\\alpha)=\\operatorname{cf}^{\\mathbf V}(\\alpha)\\bigr)\\land\n\\forall\\kappa\\in\\operatorname{Reg}^{\\mathbf V}\\;\n\\bigl((2^\\kappa)^{\\mathbf W}=F(\\kappa)\\bigr)\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}easton} \\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n(\\mathbf V,\\in)\\models_{\\mathsf{Cls}}\\mathrm{ZFC}\\mathbin{+}\\mathrm{GCH}\\land\n\\mathrm{DefinableEastonFunction}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(F,\\mathbf V)\n\\to\\exists_{\\mathsf{Cls}}\\mathbf W,\\mathbb P,G\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{EastonClassForcingExtension}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(\\mathbf W,\\mathbf V,\\mathbb P,G)\\land\n(\\mathbf W,\\in)\\models_{\\mathsf{Cls}}\\mathrm{ZFC}\\land\n\\operatorname{Ord}^{\\mathbf W}=\\operatorname{Ord}^{\\mathbf V}\\land\n\\operatorname{Card}^{\\mathbf W}=\\operatorname{Card}^{\\mathbf V}\\land\n\\forall\\alpha\\in\\operatorname{Ord}^{\\mathbf V}\\;\n\\bigl(\\operatorname{cf}^{\\mathbf W}(\\alpha)=\\operatorname{cf}^{\\mathbf V}(\\alpha)\\bigr)\\land\n\\forall\\kappa\\in\\operatorname{Reg}^{\\mathbf V}\\;\n\\bigl((2^\\kappa)^{\\mathbf W}=F(\\kappa)\\bigr)\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>This is the global class form of Easton's theorem. The earlier version called a set-function predicate on a purported set carrier <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"V\">\\(V\\)</span> while simultaneously using <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"V\">\\(V\\)</span> as the whole ground universe, and it left both satisfaction relations unbound.</li>\n<li>The lower bound <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa^+\\leq F(\\kappa)\">\\(\\kappa^+\\leq F(\\kappa)\\)</span> follows from <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa&lt;\\operatorname{cf}(F(\\kappa))\">\\(\\kappa&lt;\\operatorname{cf}(F(\\kappa))\\)</span> together with cardinal-valuedness; monotonicity and the cofinality inequality are the two Easton constraints.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md","status":"resolved","id":"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\mathbf V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbf W","display":false},{"tex":"F,\\mathbb P,G","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ZFC}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{GCH}","display":false},{"tex":"(\\mathbf V,\\in)\\models_{\\mathsf{Cls}}\\mathrm{ZFC+GCH}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{DefinableEastonFunction}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(F,\\mathbf V)","display":false},{"tex":"F","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbf V","display":false},{"tex":"\\kappa<\\operatorname{cf}^{\\mathbf V}(F(\\kappa))","display":false},{"tex":"\\kappa","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{EastonClassForcingExtension}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(\\mathbf W,\\mathbf V,\\mathbb P,G)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb P","display":false},{"tex":"F","display":false},{"tex":"G","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbf V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbf W=\\mathbf V[G]","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}easton} \\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n(\\mathbf V,\\in)\\models_{\\mathsf{Cls}}\\mathrm{ZFC}\\mathbin{+}\\mathrm{GCH}\\land\n\\mathrm{DefinableEastonFunction}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(F,\\mathbf V)\n\\to\\exists_{\\mathsf{Cls}}\\mathbf W,\\mathbb P,G\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{EastonClassForcingExtension}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(\\mathbf W,\\mathbf V,\\mathbb P,G)\\land\n(\\mathbf W,\\in)\\models_{\\mathsf{Cls}}\\mathrm{ZFC}\\land\n\\operatorname{Ord}^{\\mathbf W}=\\operatorname{Ord}^{\\mathbf V}\\land\n\\operatorname{Card}^{\\mathbf W}=\\operatorname{Card}^{\\mathbf V}\\land\n\\forall\\alpha\\in\\operatorname{Ord}^{\\mathbf V}\\;\n\\bigl(\\operatorname{cf}^{\\mathbf W}(\\alpha)=\\operatorname{cf}^{\\mathbf V}(\\alpha)\\bigr)\\land\n\\forall\\kappa\\in\\operatorname{Reg}^{\\mathbf V}\\;\n\\bigl((2^\\kappa)^{\\mathbf W}=F(\\kappa)\\bigr)\\Bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"V","display":false},{"tex":"V","display":false},{"tex":"\\kappa^+\\leq F(\\kappa)","display":false},{"tex":"\\kappa<\\operatorname{cf}(F(\\kappa))","display":false}],"bytes":2485,"backlinks":[{"id":"7a9cfbd003ad8ae1","anchor":"ref-2","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\mathrm{EastonClassForcingExtension}_{\\mathrm{meta}}(\\mathbf W,\\mathbf V,\\mathbb P,G)$ is the tame Easton-support class-forcing extension predicate from [[58-thm-easton]]"},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4128","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch14/58-thm-easton.md|58-thm-easton]]（batch14）"}],"outgoing":["a3348ed9eb6fb4e3"]}